### What steps can reproduce the bug?

This code exposes the issue:

```javascript
const input = 1751241600000;
const expectedIso = "2025-06-30T00:00:00.000Z";

const iterated = [...new Set([input])];
const actual = iterated[0];
const actualIso = new Date(actual).toISOString();

console.log(`input: ${input} (${expectedIso})`);
console.log(`set size: ${iterated.length}`);
console.log(`iterated value: ${actual} (${actualIso})`);

if (iterated.length !== 1 || actual !== input) {
  console.error("BUG: Set<number> iteration corrupted the epoch-millisecond value.");
  process.exitCode = 1;
} else {
  console.log("PASS");
}
```

### What is the expected behavior?

```
input: 1751241600000 (2025-06-30T00:00:00.000Z)
set size: 1
iterated value: 1751241600000 (2025-06-30T00:00:00.000Z)
PASS
